Licensing for Blast freezing a black hole

Copyright (c) 2026 Shoaib Akhtar and Xiao-Liang Qi

Different components use different licenses:

1. Paper, scientific supplement, and figure artwork: CC BY 4.0
   (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International).

   This applies to paper/manuscript.tex, paper/manuscript.pdf,
   paper/supplementary.tex, paper/supplementary.pdf, paper/references.bib,
   the six supplied figure assets in paper/, and these figure inputs:
   code/scripts/figures/fig3b.png
   code/scripts/figures/fig3c_formation_gate_color_map.png
   code/scripts/figures/fig3d.png

   It also applies to the authors' figure artwork reproduced from those inputs.
   Full terms: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Code and skills: MIT.

   This applies to code/ (except the three images explicitly listed above),
   skills/, and the paper/build.py build script.
   Full terms: LICENSES/MIT.txt

3. Datasets, environment files, and supporting repository documentation: MIT.

   This includes data/, environment/, supplementary/, README.md, AGENTS.md,
   CLAUDE.md, paper/README.md, and other original repository support files
   not explicitly assigned CC BY 4.0 above.
   Full terms: LICENSES/MIT.txt

Third-party material and dependencies retain their own terms. In particular,
the separately downloaded Springer Nature LaTeX class and bibliography style
are not covered by either author license. See supplementary/reuse-status.md.
The license texts retain their own applicable terms.
